{"term":"drone","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9037c9546ce94a0ae2","definition":"A male hymenopteran (ant, bee, hornet, or wasp), whose sole primary function is to mate with the queen.","example":"All with united force combine to drive / The lazy drones from the laborious hive.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebe155059864f38ae5","definition":"One who does not work; a lazy person, an idler.","example":"SHYLOCK: / The patch is kind enough, but a huge feeder, / Snail-slow in profit, and he sleeps by day / More than the wild-cat; drones hive not with me; / Therefore I part with him; and part with him / To one what I would have him help to waste / His borrowed purse. […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6ebc8ea7664410315","definition":"One who performs menial or tedious work.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["drudge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cd0cf60a1932b6e8d5","definition":"Any remotely operated or autonomous vehicle for land, sea, air, or space.","example":"aerial drones","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f720037239c1c4ee2e","definition":"A Toyota HiAce or a similar van, especially one used by Ugandan state agents to kidnap opposition members.","example":"The van is locally referred to as \"a drone\" because it is compact and stable under extreme conditions. It is also very fast. Technically though, it is a Toyota Hiace, which is usually used for commercial purposes.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Uganda","register":"Uganda","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0bf4d380f0f5b81433","definition":"One who lacks the ability to think critically and independently, especially one who follows a group blindly; a non-player character.","example":"The billionaire-friendly media drones and frenzied multiculturalist politicians are imposing \"vibrant\" third world social violence onto Australians, and Australians don't get to vote against this \"bipartisan\" conspiracy. The hyperactive globalist politicians and media drones might find themselves facing firing squads if they don't change their corrupt ways.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, slang","register":"derogatory, slang","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed97907e1578ae77f3","definition":"In dronification kink, one who is mindless and obedient to a dominant, characterized by a detached and robotic identity and an anonymous appearance, typically composed of a latex suit and gas mask.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3b48718559daa1e1e9","definition":"To kill or destroy with a drone (unmanned aircraft), or with a missile fired by a drone.","example":"\"I have a lot of advice for him,\" Ayers said in the interview, aired Tuesday night. \"I want him to stop droning people. I want him to close Guantanamo. I want universal healthcare. Don't you think we deserve universal healthcare? Seriously.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial, transitive","wordFamily":["alimony drone","antidrone","combat drone","counterdrone","drone-athon","drone-a-thon","droneboarding","drone fly","Dronehenge","droneless","dronelike","drone metal","dronepipe","dronescape","dronesome","Dronespace","drone wall","droney","dronie","dronification","dronify","dronish","dronist","dronology","drony","microdrone","minidrone","Nintendrone","office drone","suicide drone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e400953293c696b7c2","definition":"To produce a low-pitched hum or buzz.","example":"","pos":"verb","syno